MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New src/auth/effective-scopes.ts: a session's usable scopes are the
  intersection of what this MCP client's user approved at its own consent
  and what the Xero tokens behind the session carry now. A wider token set
  (for example from another client's newer consent in a shared token store)
  can never widen a client beyond its own grant; a narrower one narrows it.
- registerAllTools takes the two scope sources, registers from the
  intersection, and wraps every tool callback with a request-time re-check
  that fails closed with insufficient_scope instead of calling Xero when
  the upstream scopes changed after connection.
- index.ts passes props.scopes (this client's grant) and session.scopes
  (live token scopes) separately.
- list_granted_scopes reports client_grant_scopes, upstream_token_scopes
  and withheld_from_this_client alongside available/unavailable tools.
- Tests: 6 for the intersection rules, 8 for isolation and post-narrowing
  invocation (35 total).
